Subject: [PATCH] Start LobiumSandboxManagerService in system_server

Brings up the OS-embedded app sandbox as a platform service, before third-party
apps can start, so the first install on a fresh machine is already sandboxed.

Anchored for AOSP 14 (android-14.0.0_r*). If the surrounding lines have drifted,
apply with `git apply --3way` (or --reject) and place the traceBegin/startService
block anywhere in startOtherServices() ahead of PHASE_THIRD_PARTY_APPS_CAN_START.
---
 services/java/com/android/server/SystemServer.java | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/frameworks/base/services/java/com/android/server/SystemServer.java b/frameworks/base/services/java/com/android/server/SystemServer.java
--- a/frameworks/base/services/java/com/android/server/SystemServer.java
+++ b/frameworks/base/services/java/com/android/server/SystemServer.java
@@ -2600,6 +2600,14 @@ public final class SystemServer implements Dumpable {
                 t.traceEnd();
             }

+            // Lobium: OS-embedded app sandbox. Moves third-party apps into isolated profiles as they
+            // are installed. Started here so it is live before PHASE_THIRD_PARTY_APPS_CAN_START and the
+            // very first install on a fresh machine is caught.
+            t.traceBegin("StartLobiumSandboxManager");
+            mSystemServiceManager.startService(
+                    "com.android.server.lobium.LobiumSandboxManagerService");
+            t.traceEnd();
+
             // LneWiFi/Telephony and others depend on the above; keep late-init below this line.
             t.traceBegin("MakeVibratorServiceReady");
             try {
